[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one bug, one fix queued. The reports in it say
otherwise. Counted the desk's own way, by tenant and channel as `causes.ts` sorts them, and not by
subject line or intake tag, they fall into three problems. The queued fix closes only the first.

<Callout kind="warn">
Each problem has its own ticket below. Merging them back into #4471 hides two bugs behind one fix.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} repo="patrikbreitenmoser/support-kb" />

## Status

Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October:

- `parser`: **fixed** by `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
- `hint`: **won't fix**, the booking-v3 form is retired.
- `one-day`: not in the update. The parser fix does not touch a one-day shift.

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads every date month first.** Day-first tenants (en-GB, nl-NL,
de-DE and the rest) book 3 October and get an invite for 10 March. This is what #4471 says, and
the queued fix is for this.

**`hint`: booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field.** Tenants on booking-v3 write
the day first. Their people type what the hint tells them, month first, and the form reads it
the tenant's way. Fixing the parser does not fix this: the hint has to match the tenant's locale.

**`one-day`: the date moves by exactly one day.** Tuesday becomes Monday, every booking in June is
off by a day, a client in Lisbon and one in Toronto get different days for one meeting, an invite
arrives before the booking. Day and month are not swapped. This looks like a time zone or
daylight saving conversion. The desk noted these reports as one-day moves (`desk-notes.json`), but
`causes.ts` has no cause for them, so they stay counted under `parser` by tenant. They need
their own fix all the same.

## Why it was merged as one

- Duplicates were merged by subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
  Every report about a wrong date has a similar subject, whatever caused it.
- The intake tag is a guess from the reporter's browser. It disagrees with the tenant for many
  reports, so counting by tag gives the wrong split.
- The export comes in overlapping pages: some reports appear twice. Count by id.

## For the desk

- Before merging into a big ticket, check the cause by tenant and channel, not the subject.
- When a report does not fit a known cause, give it its own ticket, even if it is the only one.

